#: src/Mcp/Pricing.php:36
msgid "Servers and databases are pay as you go: billed by the hour, and a month never costs more than the max per month. An hour that has started counts as a whole hour, and a stopped server is still billed until it is deleted (delete_server, delete_database); billing stops in the hour the service is deleted. The hours are invoiced monthly to the customer's saved card, which is required to order (account credit alone is not enough); VAT is added on the invoice, and every price here excludes VAT. Add-ons are billed by the hour like the service and capped the same way: a database can get extra storage (it can be added later in the dashboard and only made larger) and a public IPv4 address, a server can get daily backups and one extra disk. Use price_quote for the total of a plan with add-ons. Account credit, if the customer has some, is applied first on usage invoices. Business email is a monthly subscription, plugins are yearly and domains are yearly per ending."
